{
  "id": "Compound::DB01192 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Oxymorphone is implicated in the regulation of Cyp3a4 through a series of interconnected molecular pathways. The evidence suggests that Oxymorphone binds to Cyp2d6, which then participates in steroid hydroxylase activity, ultimately leading to the participation of Cyp3a4. Similarly, Oxymorphone's binding to Cyp2d6 also leads to the participation of Cyp3a4 through a different pathway involving steroid hydroxylase activity. This indicates that Oxymorphone exerts a modulatory effect on Cyp3a4 via the Cyp2d6 enzyme, which is involved in the metabolism of steroid hormones. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Oxymorphone to Cyp3a4 underscores the complexity of the interaction, but the consistent involvement of Cyp2d6 as a bridge between Oxymorphone and Cyp3a4 provides a robust mechanistic link. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Cyp2d6 in mediating Oxymorphone's influence on Cyp3a4, suggesting that Oxymorphone may modulate Cyp3a4 activity through the metabolic conversion of steroid hormones.",
